      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing AWS Transcribe**\n\nI've decided to move forward with AWS Transcribe for the transcription provider. I'm focusing on creating the Python file, `poll_transcription.py`, which will specifically handle polling a transcription job and retrieving the transcript. Now I can start to develop the core structure.\n\n\n**Developing Core Logic**\n\nI'm currently fleshing out the `poll_transcription.py` script. The essential structure is taking shape, centered around a function that polls the AWS Transcribe job. My focus now is on integrating the `boto3` library to interface with Transcribe and handle job status checks. Next, I will consider how to securely handle AWS credentials within the program's execution environment.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789821397706,
          "start": 1789821394498
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b9ab1e42001nUTJ36hh3MSabU",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9ab19da001ADa2eDNKO2FkrL",
      "session_id": "ses_f4654e635ffeGOEhG1nBmXgOz3",
      "time_created": 1789821394498,
      "time_updated": 1789821397706
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "aQhFCSHvunAXK1je",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "\nimport time\nimport requests\nimport boto3\n\ndef poll_transcription_job(job_name, region_name='us-east-1'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Polls an AWS Transcribe transcription job and returns the transcript.\n\n    Args:\n        job_name (str): The name of the transcription job.\n        region_name (str): The AWS region where the job was created.\n\n    Returns:\n        str: The transcript if the job is successful, None otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    transcribe_client = boto3.client('transcribe', region_name=region_name)\n\n    while True:\n        response = transcribe_client.get_transcription_job(TranscriptionJobName=job_name)\n        job_status = response['TranscriptionJob']['TranscriptionJobStatus']\n\n        if job_status == 'COMPLETED':\n            transcript_uri = response['TranscriptionJob']['Transcript']['TranscriptFileUri']\n            # Fetch the transcript content from the URI\n            transcript_content = requests.get(transcript_uri).text\n            return transcript_content\n        elif job_status == 'FAILED':\n            print(f\"Transcription job {job_name} failed.\")\n            return None\n        else:\n            print(f\"Transcription job {job_name} is {job_status}. Waiting...\")\n            time.sleep(10)  # Wait for 10 seconds before polling again\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Example usage (replace with your actual job name and region)\n    # To run this, you would first need to start a transcription job\n    # using transcribe_client.start_transcription_job(...)\n    # and then provide the job name here.\n    example_job_name = \"my-example-transcription-job\"\n    transcript = poll_transcription_job(example_job_name)\n\n    if transcript:\n        print(\"\\nTranscription Complete:\")\n        print(transcript)\n    else:\n        print(\"\\nFailed to retrieve transcript.\")\n",
            "filePath": "poll_transcription.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "diagnostics": {},
            "exists": false,
