      "data": {
        "text": "**Developing Transcription Script**\n\nI've created the `poll_transcription.py` script. It leverages AWS Transcribe and includes `boto3` for AWS interaction and `requests` for fetching transcript content. My new function, `poll_transcription_job`, now takes a job name and URI to streamline the process.\n\n\n**Finalizing Functionality and Integration**\n\nI've finalized `poll_transcription.py`. It's fully functional with AWS Transcribe and leverages `boto3` and `requests`. The `poll_transcription_job` function is now clean, taking only the job name. Polling with `time.sleep` handles job status (COMPLETED/FAILED). I retrieve the `TranscriptFileUri` and its content, and an example usage block is included. The provider is clearly AWS via `boto3.client('transcribe')` and relevant terms.\n\n\n",
